class Solution {
public:
    bool containsDuplicate(vector<int>& nums) {
        int n= nums.size();
        sort(nums.begin(),nums.end());
        int i=0; int j=1;
        while(i<n && j<n){
            if(nums[i]==nums[j]){
                return true;
            }
           i++; j++;
        }
        return false;
    }

}; 




#### Contains Duplicate

**Intuition:**
Sort the array so duplicate elements come together.
Then compare every pair of adjacent elements.
If any adjacent elements are equal, a duplicate exists.

**Algorithm:**
Sort the array.
Use two pointers to check adjacent elements.
Return `true` if a duplicate is found, otherwise `false`.

**Complexity:**
Time: **O(n log n)**
Space: **O(1)**
